        "body_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Brass Hardware</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Brass contains small percentages of lead to enhance its properties, making it suitable for various manufacturing processes. We use a range of traditional&nbsp;and modern manufacturing techniques that require varying alloys of brass.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Brass Taps</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>All of our brass taps comply with NSF/ANSI 61 standards.&nbsp;</p><p>NSF/ANSI 61 is an American National Standard developed by the National Sanitation Foundation (NSF)&nbsp;and the American National Standards Institute (ANSI).&nbsp;NSF/ANSI 61 focuses on the health effects of products, components, and materials that come into contact with drinking water.&nbsp;NSF/ANSI 61 certification provides peace of mind to consumers by indicating which products&nbsp;are safe for use in drinking water systems.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Furniture</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Our carcasses and shelves are made from high-quality birch-veneered plywood which gives excellent rigidity.</p><p>The plywood used in our furniture is CARB Phase 2 compliant.&nbsp;</p><p>CARB 2 is a regulation created by the California Air Resources Board (CARB). The board created this as a way to prevent formaldehyde from being released into the air and reducing the air quality.</p><p>The CARB phase 2 certification signifies that the product releases a low enough amount of formaldehyde to be considered safe.</p><p>Any formaldehyde released by products with a CARB phase 2 compliant seal is a small enough amount that it has absolutely no risk to your health.</p>"
          }
        }
